ARM PrimeCell Generic Install Script
------------------------------------

This directory contains the INSTALL script required to build the
correct directory structure for an ARM PrimeCell from a distribution.

The script should be run in-place, i.e. from this directory.

USAGE : INSTALL <PLnum> <release> [<PLnum> <release>] <destination>

This script will unpack the specified ARM PrimeCell deliverables
into the directory <destination>.

<PLnum> should be the ARM Code for the PrimeCell to be unpacked,
for example "PL170"

<release> should be the release version to be unpacked, e.g. "REL2v1"

<destination> should be the directory into which you want the
distribution unpacked.  If the destination directory already
exists, any files overwritten by this new distribution will be
renamed to include a ".bak" extension.

For example,

    ./INSTALL PL170 REL2v1 /arm/primecells


Important Notice about "tar"
----------------------------

Some PrimeCells are released as a set of tar files.  In this case, the
script will untar these to create the installation.

In order for this to work without complication, the tool will attempt to
locate a GNU tar executable that is at least version 1.13.  Other tar
executables are known to cause problems when unpacking large distributions.

If you do not have a compatible version on your path, you can force the
installation script to use a particular executable by specifying it in the
"FORCE_TAR_EXE" environment variable, as in:

    setenv FORCE_TAR_EXE /path/to/my/gnutar

If you do not have GNU tar installed on your network, we recommend that
you do so to avoid problems.  For more information about this program and
where you can download it, open the following URL in your web browser:

    http://www.gnu.org/software/tar/tar.html


Please report any problems with this script to support-primecell@arm.com
